-- stderr --
costroid: printed a patch for .github/workflows/review.yml, and wrote nothing
Apply it from the repository's root with git apply. Your job keeps the
permissions it has, and the read step asks for nothing more. The report job
holds checks: write and pull-requests: write, runs on pull requests alone, and
runs nothing the pull request wrote. docs/existing-workflow.md says more. The
patch adds --max-budget-usd 5 to the claude_args of the claude-code-action step,
so Claude Code stops a run once its own estimate passes USD 5, and gives the
read step and the report job that cap. To change the cap, change it in
claude_args, in claude-args and in both budget-usd inputs.
