== the platform: exit 0
-- stdout --
--- a/.github/workflows/review.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/review.yml
@@ -25,3 +25,47 @@
             Review this pull request.
 
             List the bugs.
+          claude_args: --max-budget-usd 5
+        id: claude
+      - name: Read what the run cost
+        if: always() && steps.claude.outputs.execution_file != ''
+        uses: Costroid/costroid/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 # v1.0.0-alpha.10
+        with:
+          stage: read
+          post-review: "true"
+          execution-file: ${{ steps.claude.outputs.execution_file }}
+          budget-usd: "5"
+          claude-args: --max-budget-usd 5
+          billing-account: ${{ github.repository_owner }}
+
+  report:
+    needs: review
+    if: always() && github.event_name == 'pull_request'
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
+    timeout-minutes: 5
+    permissions:
+      checks: write
+      contents: read
+      pull-requests: write
+    steps:
+      - uses: Costroid/costroid/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 # v1.0.0-alpha.10
+        with:
+          stage: report
+          post-review: "true"
+          budget-usd: "5"
+          agent-result: ${{ needs.review.result }}
+
+  ingest:
+    needs: review
+    if: always() && needs.review.result != 'skipped' && vars.COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL != ''
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
+    timeout-minutes: 5
+    permissions:
+      id-token: write
+    steps:
+      - uses: Costroid/costroid/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 # v1.0.0-alpha.10
+        with:
+          stage: ingest
+          platform-url: ${{ vars.COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL }}
+          installation-id: github-owner:${{ github.repository_owner_id }}
+          platform-token: ${{ secrets.COSTROID_PLATFORM_TOKEN }}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/costroid-connect.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Binds this repository's owner to its Costroid Platform tenant, so the ingest
+# job of an agent recipe can send rows there. docs/connect.md says what the
+# proof is and what it binds.
+name: costroid-connect
+
+on:
+  # GitHub runs a schedule from the default branch only, so the platform takes
+  # its proof whatever the branch rules are. A binding stays current for 7 days
+  # after its last proof, and a daily run renews it.
+  schedule:
+    - cron: "23 5 * * *"
+  # A push to the default branch binds at once when that branch is protected.
+  push:
+
+permissions: {}
+
+jobs:
+  connect:
+    if: >-
+      vars.COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL != ''
+      && (github.event_name == 'schedule'
+      || github.ref == format('refs/heads/{0}', github.event.repository.default_branch))
+    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
+    timeout-minutes: 5
+    permissions:
+      # The proof is the job's OIDC token, issued for the tenant's audience.
+      id-token: write
+    steps:
+      - uses: Costroid/costroid/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 # v1.0.0-alpha.10
+        with:
+          stage: install
+      - name: Bind the owner
+        env:
+          COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL: ${{ vars.COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL }}
+          COSTROID_PLATFORM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.COSTROID_PLATFORM_TOKEN }}
+        run: costroid connect --platform-url "$COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL"
-- stderr --
costroid: printed a patch for .github/workflows/review.yml and .github/workflows/costroid-connect.yml, and wrote nothing
Apply it from the repository's root with git apply. Your job keeps the
permissions it has, and the read step asks for nothing more. The report job
holds checks: write and pull-requests: write, runs on pull requests alone, and
runs nothing the pull request wrote. docs/existing-workflow.md says more. The
patch adds --max-budget-usd 5 to the claude_args of the claude-code-action step,
so Claude Code stops a run once its own estimate passes USD 5, and gives the
read step and the report job that cap. To change the cap, change it in
claude_args, in claude-args and in both budget-usd inputs.

The ingest job holds id-token: write and reads the platform's address from a
repository variable. Set it with:
  gh variable set COSTROID_PLATFORM_URL --body https://app.costroid.com
The ingest job sends the rows once the integration token is set as
COSTROID_PLATFORM_TOKEN and the owner is bound to the platform. The workflow
costroid-connect.yml binds it from the default branch, on a push when that
branch is protected and on its daily schedule otherwise. docs/connect.md says
how.
